WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.635
-Hello, everyone, and
welcome back to the attic.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.871
I never, ever anticipated
that I'd be doing my show

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.574
not in a television studio
but in quiet solitude

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.142
in my attic,
slowly descending

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.778
into an ever-deepening chasm
of infinite madness.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:15.314
But all things considered,
I really have grown to like it.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.416
You know,
there's a magical quality

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.485
to this attic,
as evidenced by the fact

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.620
that my beloved copy
of "The Thorn Birds"

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.491
has multiplied and mutated into
anagrams of itself,

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:27.760
unpublished sequels,
similar-sounding titles.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.831
and even other literary classics
with a "Thorn Bird" twist.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.632
And let's be clear --
that's magic.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.101
That's not something I'm doing,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.270
because it would be
a colossal waste of time.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.806
The door behind me
has provided entry

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.041
to not only wasps and firemen

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.144
but Academy Award nominee
Ethan Hawke,

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.711
leading some to ask, "Seth,

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.213
have you ever thought
of going through that door?"

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:50.416
And, yeah, the door does speak
and beckon for my entry,

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.552
but, I assure you, I have
no interest in finding out

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.387
where it leads,
and I certainly will not

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.888
be lured by its siren call.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.824
And speaking of
ignoring things, -- segue --

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.592
the President has decided
to inhabit

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.928
an alternate reality
where the coronavirus pandemic

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.163
just doesn't exist,
even as the U.S.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.366
sets a single-day record
for new cases.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.934
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:12.505
[ "A Closer Look"
theme music plays ]

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.541
An undeniable lesson
of the Trump era has been

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.208
that one of our two major
political parties

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:19.311
is filled with
mentally unwell weirdos.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.013
Yesterday, for example,
at hearing

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.583
on Attorney General Bill Barr's
various abuses of power,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.384
GOP Congressman Louie Gohmert

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:28.187
tried to drown out
a witness's testimony

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.689
by banging the table,
and he wouldn't stop.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:33.159
[ Tapping ]
-This conduct in particular

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.395
gives cause for great concern
about what Barr may do next.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.831
Just one -- one --
another 30 seconds.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.900
In closing, it needs to be said

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.269
that Bill Barr
does regularly lie

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.805
in ways that impact
official action.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.374
Along with his continuing
media project

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.410
to make Americans believe
that the FBI conspired

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.878
against Donald Trump...

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.280
-The witness will continue.
[ Tapping continues ]

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.282
-Can I have one more sentence?
-By all means.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.517
-Okay.
[ Tapping continues ]

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.752
But, to me,
Barr's crowning dishonesty

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.654
is the portrait of
Edward Levy that --

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:05.958
-Mr. Chairman, I would ask
that the sergeant-at-arms

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:10.295
be called upon to stop
the disruption of this meeting.

00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:11.931
[ Tapping continues ]

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.232
I can't hear this witness.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.901
This is
a very important witness.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.836
-Yeah, well, he's
well beyond the time.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.772
-The Chair has the authority --
-If there are no rules about --

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.675
There's no rules
about when you can make noise.

00:02:23.675 --> 00:02:25.310
-Ah, well-played, sir.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:28.547
There aren't any rules
about when you can make noise.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.517
And what a good point
for a 66-year-old man to make.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.818
You know, there's
also not a rule

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:34.888
saying you can't interrupt
a witness' testimony

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.389
by streaking across
the House floor

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.890
in a giant foam cowboy hat.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.092
You go, 'Mert! [Gohmert]

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:41.594
If he's gonna be
this irritating,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.096
can we at least get him
a Hector Salamanca bell?

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.265
I mean, they do have
the same haircut.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.168
That knockapalooza really is
one of the most childish things

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.570
I've ever seen in Congress,
and this is a place

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.473
where senators have brought
snowballs onto the Senate floor,

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.242
read "Green Eggs and Ham,"

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.778
and printed out a giant poster
of Michael Cohen's face

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.880
that said,
"Liar, liar, pants on fire!"

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.683
Congress is like some sort of
Montessori daycare

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.218
where, for 40 grand a year,

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.687
your child is supervised
by other children.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.122
"We like to think of it
not as a daycare

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:11.357
but as a community.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.993
Good job with the
knife-juggling, Ashley.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.327
Be who you are.
Oh, God.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:17.897
Oh, that's a -- that's a lot of
blood over there."

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.732
So, that's what a Republican
member of Congress was doing

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:23.336
on the day when the U.S. set
a new single-day record

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.638
for coronavirus infections.
And what about the President?

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.508
He was tweeting about --
you guessed it -- lobsters.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.018
Cool. So, if you're one of
the 40 million people

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.386
who lost their job
during the pandemic,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.154
and had to wait in line
for unemployment,

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.022
just jump in a boat
and catch some lobster.

00:03:44.022 --> 00:03:45.792
Instead of a second stimulus
check in the mail,

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.360
every American is gonna get
a fishing net

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.995
and a pair of rubber boots.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.430
But you got to be suspicious

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.098
when Trump tweets
a bunch of nice things

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.600
about your industry
out of nowhere.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.668
It's like getting flowers
from your husband

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.003
on a regular Tuesday morning.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.972
Your first thought has to be,
"What did you do?"

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.340
Well, it won't surprise you
to learn

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.708
that Trump is lying
about this, too.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.443
And when you can lie
about lobster,

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:06.813
the sky is the limit.
Next, he's gonna tweet...

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.752
In reality,
lobster exports plunged

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:16.322
after Trump took office,
thanks to his trade war.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.607
Of course Trump is lying.
If he really thought

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.141
he'd made lobstering
so profitable,

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:37.977
he'd be going from
restaurant to restaurant,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.479
plunging his hands
into lobster tanks,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.946
trying to steal
as many as he could.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:42.682
"Damn you, you son of a bitch.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.483
Keep those pincers away from me.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.352
This lobster is Antifa."

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.855
So, a Republican Congressman
was banging on tables,

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.957
and the president was lying
about lobster

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.192
as the U.S.
was setting a new record

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.760
for coronavirus infections,

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.595
five months after
our first official case.

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.631
Remember, at the beginning
of this outbreak,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.733
when you heard the phrase
"flatten the curve"

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.002
over and over again,
like you were watching

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.336
a Billy Blanks workout video?

00:05:04.336 --> 00:05:05.370
"Come on, everyone,

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.973
two knee raises
into a side kick.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.907
Tae Bo is all about
flattening those curves!"

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:10.643
That's why we all
stayed in our homes,

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.811
watching "Maury,"

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.179
and drinking cereal
straight out of the bowl,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.347
in our sweatpants
for three months.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:17.816
The point was to get cases and
hospitalizations

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:21.119
down to a manageable level and
to limit community transmission

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:22.788
so we could get
a rigorous system

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:25.224
of testing and contact tracing
in place

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.426
that would allow us
to safely get back

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:28.928
to some semblance of normalcy.

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:31.330
Instead, the president
has squandered all of that,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.065
complained that testing
makes him look bad,

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.535
and called on his government
to slow testing down.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.904
And now his administration
is following through,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.738
cutting funding to testing sites

00:05:39.738 --> 00:05:41.907
as the outbreak reaches
its worst levels yet.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:43.776
-There's a new plan
at the White House

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.744
for how to deal with
coronavirus testing

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:48.280
at the federal level
in states across the country.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.483
Geoff Bennett reporting
that the Trump administration

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.785
is planning to end
its funding and support

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:55.687
for coronavirus testing sites at
the end of this month.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.022
That is, on June 30th.

00:05:57.022 --> 00:05:59.058
-That's right, they're cutting
federal funding

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.793
for community testing sites now,
as the outbreak hits a new peak.

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:04.063
That's like a pilot turning off
the "seat belt" sign

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.032
after they graze a mountain.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.966
"Don't worry, folks, we just
nicked one of the Rockies.

00:06:07.966 --> 00:06:10.102
Feel free to stretch your legs,
and don't look out the window.

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.171
I assure you that
at least half of our wings

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.806
are still attached
to the plane."

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.974
At what point can we say

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.042
Trump is actively putting people
in harm's way?

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:19.678
He holds indoor rallies,
refuses to wear a mask,

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:21.647
and wants to cut back
on testing.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.081
Soon, he's gonna start going
door-to-door,

00:06:23.081 --> 00:06:24.650
coughing on people
and licking their doorknobs.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.251
Just yesterday, it was reported

00:06:26.251 --> 00:06:28.854
that dozens of Secret Service
officers and agents

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.957
were told to self-quarantine
after Trump's Tulsa rally.

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:33.826
Trump is a one-man
superspreader.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:36.361
He is the "Ozark" swimming pool
of human beings.

00:06:36.361 --> 00:06:38.931
That's why his Secret Service
code name is Typhoid Gary.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.566
"Typhoon Gary is on the move.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.202
Well, less of a move.
It's more of a lumber."

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.771
Trump has said repeatedly,
since the day this all started,

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:48.240
that he dislikes testing,
because it makes him look bad.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.442
And even after his staff tried
to claim he was joking,

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:51.777
he corrected them

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:54.247
and said he was serious
about slowing down testing.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:04.724
-I don't kid.

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:07.993
By having more tests,
we find more cases.

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:11.564
Therefore, we test, we're
gonna have more cases.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:14.634
By having more cases,
it sounds bad.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.068
-It sounds bad because it's bad.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:18.471
Look, man, if you don't like
the sound a smoke alarm makes,

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.940
stop putting giant balls
of aluminum foil

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.141
in the microwave.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.676
"But I need to
keep my foil ball warm."

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.578
If we stop testing for cases,

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:28.080
that doesn't mean
the cases aren't there.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.682
That just means
we don't know about them.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.084
You can go into
a roadside motel room

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.652
without a black light,

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:36.022
but it doesn't mean the linens
are springtime fresh.

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:37.690
So now our curve
is headed back up

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.125
after months of Americans
making tremendous sacrifices

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.027
to try to flatten it.
Meanwhile, there are lots of

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:45.197
other countries that really did
flatten their curves.

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:46.599
Just look at
the European Union

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:49.135
or the dozens of countries
that have successfully

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:50.469
suppressed their outbreaks.

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:52.137
-The first group
is the countries

00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:54.207
that appear to have
successfully suppressed

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:55.508
transmission of the disease.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.743
That curve has come
all the way down

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.646
so that they are barely
registering any new cases.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:05.818
We have Andorra, Australia,
Austria, Bhutan, Cambodia,

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:13.091
China, Croatia, Cuba, Djibouti,
Estonia, Greece, Iceland,

00:08:13.091 --> 00:08:20.266
Jamaica, Jordan, Kosovo, Latvia,
Lebanon, Liechtenstein,

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:26.572
Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta,
Mauritius, Monaco, Montenegro,

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:34.346
New Zealand, Slovakia, Slovenia,
South Korea, Taiwan, Thailand,

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:37.482
Tunisia, and finally Vietnam.

00:08:37.482 --> 00:08:39.218
-Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
Slow down.

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:42.087
Hey, honey, what would you think
about moving to Mauritius?

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.922
You always said
you like the sand.

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:45.657
You like the sand, honey.

00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:47.859
Sounds like a list of countries
Jay Leno would ask

00:08:47.859 --> 00:08:49.862
a bunch of spring breakers
to find on a map.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.764
"Un, where's, uh, Djibouti?"

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:54.599
"Right here, baby!
There's Djibouti."

00:08:54.599 --> 00:08:56.135
We even did worse than Iceland,

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.937
a country that has
a penis museum

00:08:57.937 --> 00:09:01.040
and where -- and this is true --
people still believe in elves.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.342
The only mythical creatures
we have are Pasta Goblins.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.344
"Finish your rotini, Anthony,
or the Pasta Goblin

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:06.812
will come and steal your neck."

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:08.514
Yeah, that is a callback to
yesterday's "Closer Look."

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:09.815
I mean, I'm guessing

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.416
it's the same people
who watch every night, right?

00:09:11.416 --> 00:09:13.752
Anyway, if this is your first
look," welcome aboard.

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.353
We used have to have
an audience.

00:09:15.353 --> 00:09:17.557
America could have been
like one those countries.

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.225
In fact, some of them
have been able

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.727
to restore the cultural markers
of normalcy we all crave,

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:25.030
like live sports,
with fans in attendance.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.666
-This is a welcome sight
for sports fans.

00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:30.636
No social distancing
and no masks,

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.904
as 43,000 fans
were in the stadium

00:09:32.904 --> 00:09:35.140
for a rugby match
in New Zealand.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.343
The country had
remarkable success

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:39.011
eliminating the coronavirus.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:41.680
This weekend's match
marked a big milestone.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.082
No new cases of the virus
have been reported

00:09:44.082 --> 00:09:45.451
in more than three weeks.

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:48.888
-New Zealand had fans in
attendance at a rugby match.

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:51.256
Meanwhile, the NBA is planning
on trapping its players

00:09:51.256 --> 00:09:52.891
at Disney World like
a family stuck

00:09:52.891 --> 00:09:54.727
on a three-hour line
for Space Mountain.

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.129
"I told you we shouldn't have
wasted a FastPass

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:59.031
on Journey Into Imagination,
Lebron.

00:09:59.031 --> 00:10:00.499
I told you."

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.134
We could have been
like New Zealand.

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.802
They're going to
live sporting events

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:05.871
and eating nachos in the sun,
while we're stuck here

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:07.039
with President Lobster,

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.774
trekking to Trader Joe's
every two weeks

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:10.776
in a beekeeper's suit
stuffed with Clorox wipes.

00:10:10.776 --> 00:10:13.545
"If I don't make it back, don't
forget, microwave the mail."

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.815
Because our outbreak
is actually getting worse.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:18.283
We just set a new record,
and the peak is now higher

00:10:18.283 --> 00:10:20.386
than it was back in April,
despite the fact

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:22.421
that Trump and his team
repeatedly told us

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.523
they had succeeded
in flattening the curve.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:26.058
-We've flattened the curve

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:27.960
and really made
tremendous progress.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.961
-I'm proud to report to you,
as the head of

00:10:29.961 --> 00:10:31.797
the White House
Coronavirus Task Force,

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:34.766
we slowed the spread,
we flattened the curve.

00:10:34.766 --> 00:10:37.069
-I think you'll see, by June,
a lot of the country

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:39.037
should be back to normal,
and the hope is

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:41.406
that, by July, the country is
really rocking again.

00:10:41.406 --> 00:10:43.141
-Is there anything less
"rocking"

00:10:43.141 --> 00:10:45.177
than hearing Jared Kushner
say "rocking?"

00:10:45.177 --> 00:10:47.146
If James Hetfield said,
"Are you ready to rock?"

00:10:47.146 --> 00:10:48.714
and then Jared Kushner
came onstage,

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.416
fans would tear the place
to the ground.

00:10:50.416 --> 00:10:52.818
What even constitutes
rocking for Kushner?

00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:55.154
A second glass of rosé
on the catamaran?

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:57.122
Let's just face facts.
Jared is Steff

00:10:57.122 --> 00:10:59.191
from "Pretty in Pink,"
with worse hair.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.093
Because, Steff,
you were a real a-hole.

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:04.663
But with hair like that,
I just can't stay mad.

00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:07.766
Wait, would I like Kushner
if he had Steff hair?

00:11:07.766 --> 00:11:09.167
No! Take it away.

00:11:09.167 --> 00:11:12.437
And that's a second callback
to yesterday's "Closer Look"

00:11:12.437 --> 00:11:14.974
Trump has decided to just ignore
and, even worse,

00:11:14.974 --> 00:11:17.142
actively cover up
a national catastrophe

00:11:17.142 --> 00:11:19.912
that is only getting worse,
despite months of sacrifices

00:11:19.912 --> 00:11:22.014
by Americans who endured
tremendous pain.

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:24.649
There's no way to conclude
anything other than the fact

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:27.586
that the president is actively
putting Americans in harm's way

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:29.655
to serve his own narrow
political agenda.

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:32.557
It's true, even though...
-It sounds bad.

00:11:32.557 --> 00:11:34.760
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.796
Papa.

00:11:39.297 --> 00:11:41.734 line:0%
[ "A Closer Look"
theme music plays ]

00:11:43.268 --> 00:11:45.604 line:0%
As New York works hard
to open under phase 2,

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:47.606 line:0%
remember that we're still
a city in crisis,

00:11:47.606 --> 00:11:49.241 line:0%
and City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:50.742 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:11:50.742 --> 00:11:53.011 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:56.115 line:0%
Stay safe, wash your hands.
We love you.

